  "paletteNote": "Sixteen canon colours, not forty. SS1.3.1 caps a character at 16 including the outline; the cap is a quality lever, not a filesize one - a small deliberate ramp is what separates authored art from a gradient. Spans B0 (mortar, the outline: darkest value of the material, never pure black) through B5 (cope on the blade edge, goldHot on the trim), so SS1.3.3 three-band minimum holds in every frame. Wine carries the body, steel the plate and greatsword, gold the threshold trim, bone the cloth.\ncope and goldHot were briefly cut to chase a highlight budget, and the sheet got worse: with no bright steel the blade mapped into bone instead, which is both brighter AND the wrong material. SS3.2.5 ranks the player weapon specular second only to the hit flash, so a bright blade is correct. See the b5-mass gate note in tools/art/gates.ts.",
